{"id": "EUVD-2026-71263", "enisaUuid": "4ad0a23d-7a1d-3ae6-8fd7-404ca5b46fea", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvmet: pci-epf: put CQ ref on create_cq mapping failure\n\nnvmet_pci_epf_create_cq() calls nvmet_cq_create(), which takes a\nreference on the controller and installs the completion queue. If the\nsubsequent PCI address-space mapping fails or returns a too-small partial\nmapping, the function jumps to err_internal / err_unmap_queue without\ncalling nvmet_cq_put(). The matching put in nvmet_pci_epf_delete_cq() is\ngated on NVMET_PCI_EPF_Q_LIVE, which is only set after the mapping\nsucceeds, so teardown never releases these references. A remote PCI host\nthat drives Create IO CQ commands with a failing PRP1/pci_addr therefore\nleaks the CQ and a controller reference on each attempt.\n\nDrop the CQ reference on the mapping-failure paths. The err_internal and\nerr_unmap_queue labels are only reachable after nvmet_cq_create() has\nsucceeded, so this pairs the create/put correctly.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:27:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:44:13", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f31650243c1ab32394077f234685e89ed8dece84", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5f97fae2503a763fa0f953abf5f121b0fef7d0d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/56a7b6a6880dbabe28214ff88df8d229ca3a944a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/659ae9d02cb5d72c76f74fff7441eb8fb64d8f5c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xgj8-pp4r-hmxg", "CVE-2026-80821"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0058cc94-05c5-3ea7-840a-df6d5bcf9170", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14"}, {"id": "152f6c28-c188-3a31-a983-b2c186d1a3bc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0faa0fe6f90ea59b10d1b0f15ce0eb0c18eff186 <b5f97fae2503a763fa0f953abf5f121b0fef7d0d"}, {"id": "2124aea7-4b6f-33bb-b1ca-a9b8ee674517", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "515118e3-563b-34ae-b3b1-802959074a9d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.1"}, {"id": "827a5fa9-59b4-3e46-9f21-d00ecfc3845a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0faa0fe6f90ea59b10d1b0f15ce0eb0c18eff186 <659ae9d02cb5d72c76f74fff7441eb8fb64d8f5c"}, {"id": "8dfeb1f0-8d11-31bc-952b-288c49d521b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.11"}, {"id": "915724ca-94fa-357d-ab25-731d5df2f61b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.47"}, {"id": "aa353021-89ef-3527-b257-b02e81d78fdc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "cae86be9-0203-38e6-8bfb-5960ae795c45", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0faa0fe6f90ea59b10d1b0f15ce0eb0c18eff186 <56a7b6a6880dbabe28214ff88df8d229ca3a944a"}, {"id": "dc1754a4-3f04-3930-81de-df986c6587ab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0faa0fe6f90ea59b10d1b0f15ce0eb0c18eff186 <f31650243c1ab32394077f234685e89ed8dece84"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "662b9919-15ed-363b-a70d-82f2024cab6e", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}